grateful|thankful|ADJECTIVE|feeling thanks for help or benefit|Feeling or showing thanks for something helpful or beneficial.|biết ơn; cảm kích|We were grateful for the neighbours' help with the move.|Chúng tôi biết ơn sự giúp đỡ của hàng xóm khi chuyển nhà.|Grateful to a person for something; grateful for a benefit. Not the same as pleased that something exists.|0
liquid|fluid-substance|NOUN|substance that flows and takes its container's shape|A substance that flows and takes the shape of its container rather than keeping a fixed shape.|chất lỏng|She poured the liquid carefully into a narrow bottle.|Cô ấy cẩn thận rót chất lỏng vào một chai cổ hẹp.|Countable for a type of substance; uncountable in quantities such as a litre of liquid.|0
liquid|fluid-state|ADJECTIVE|in a flowing physical state|In a physical state that can flow and take the shape of a container.|ở thể lỏng; dạng lỏng|The wax was still liquid when he poured it into the mould.|Sáp vẫn ở dạng lỏng khi anh ấy đổ vào khuôn.|Before a material noun or after a linking verb; liquid here describes physical state, not financial availability.|1
performance|presentation|NOUN|presentation of an artistic work|An occasion when people present music, drama, or another artistic work to an audience.|buổi biểu diễn; màn trình diễn|The performance ended with a song by the whole cast.|Buổi biểu diễn kết thúc bằng một bài hát của toàn bộ diễn viên.|Countable; a performance of a work names what is presented.|0
performance|how-well-working|NOUN|quality of someone's work or operation|How well a person, machine, or system carries out an activity.|hiệu suất; mức độ thực hiện|The new battery improved the camera's performance.|Pin mới cải thiện hiệu suất hoạt động của máy ảnh.|Usually uncountable for quality of operation; performance in a task identifies the context.|1
strand|thin-length|NOUN|single thin length of material|A single thin length of something such as hair, thread, or wire.|sợi|A strand of hair had caught on the scarf.|Một sợi tóc mắc vào chiếc khăn quàng.|Countable; a strand of specifies the material, while strands is the plural.|0
strand|one-part|NOUN|one connected part of a larger whole|One part or line of activity within a larger, interconnected whole.|mảng; phần; nhánh nội dung|The project combines a research strand with public workshops.|Dự án kết hợp một mảng nghiên cứu với các buổi hội thảo công cộng.|Countable; a strand of a project or argument names a connected component, not a physical fibre.|1
whose|question-with-noun|DETERMINER|asking who owns something|Used before a noun to ask which person owns or is associated with something.|của ai|Whose bag is beside the door?|Chiếc túi cạnh cửa là của ai?|Question determiner before a noun; whose is a possession word, while who's means who is or who has.|0
whose|question-alone|PRONOUN|asking the owner without repeating the noun|Used to ask who owns something when the thing is already understood.|của ai|Several coats are here; whose is this?|Ở đây có vài chiếc áo khoác; chiếc này là của ai?|Standalone question pronoun; no noun follows whose in this construction.|1
whose|relative-possession|DETERMINER|linking a person or thing to a possession|Used to connect a person or thing with something belonging or related to it.|có; mà của người đó hoặc vật đó|We met a writer whose stories are set by the sea.|Chúng tôi gặp một nhà văn có những câu chuyện lấy bối cảnh bên biển.|Relative determiner before a noun; can refer to people or things and does not require an apostrophe.|2
